<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">News Discernment and Humans.</h3>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ground the study empirically, we first replicate the correlation analysis of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Calvillo et al. (2021)</a></cite>, recomputing Pearson coefficients between each Big-Five trait and news discernment (Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In News Discernment and Belief in Misinformation. ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Evaluating the Simulation of Human Personality-Driven Susceptibility to Misinformation with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). This reproducibility check generates the five-element reference vector that serves as our human baseline; only after establishing it do we query the LLMs, so any divergence reflects simulation limits rather than analytic drift.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ News Discernment and Humans. ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Evaluating the Simulation of Human Personality-Driven Susceptibility to Misinformation with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports the two-tailed correlations (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>): News discernment is positively related to Agreeableness (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>), Conscientiousness (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.026" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.026</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.026</annotation></semantics></math>), and Open-Mindedness (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>). No significant correlations are found with Extraversion (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.271" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.271</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.271</annotation></semantics></math>) or Negative emotionality (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.764" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.764</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.764</annotation></semantics></math>). Inter-trait correlations are included for completeness.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Replication of human findings using data from Calvillo et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Calvillo et al. (2021)</a></cite>.</span> Pearson correlation coefficients between news discernment and personality traits. Significance levels: * <math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.05</annotation></semantics></math>, ** <math id="S4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.01</annotation></semantics></math>, *** <math id="S4.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;.001</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:83.2pt;vertical-align:-39.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-4.2pt,1.0pt) scale(0.976490930068793,0.976490930068793) ;">
